Z||000000||FieroLisa||03-10-2001||01:57 AM||||What's the best way to clean a car cover? Any tips? <P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>Tarheels Fieros Website</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||deceler8||03-10-2001||10:55 AM||||If the box it came in says it's machine washable, throw it in the washer.<P>My guess is that you'll ruin it if you try to dry it in a dryer. And you'd probably be advised to use the gentle cycle.<P>Or hand wash it in the bathtub.<P>I use a surplus parachute to cover my antique truck and when it gets dirty, it goes into the washing machine.||||reg||1
Z||000002||LarryB||03-10-2001||11:24 AM||||I wouldn't machine wash it, hand washing is kinder to the cover. <P>If there's a lot of junk stuck to it you'll need to first lay it out on the (clean) driveway and hose it off then gently scrub it with a soft brush and soapy water.  If you've ever washed a canvas boat cover or awning the idea is similar except you shouldn't be as agressive in scrubbing the car cover.<P>If there's mold or mildew on the cover add some bleach to the soapy water - you don't need a huge amount - and work it a bit using the brush around where the black spots are.  The goal is to 'work in' the bleach water into the spores and kill them (so the problem doesn't get any worse) and get off the loose stuff, not to scrub off the spots.<P>If its fairly clean to begin with or you want to make sure you get it really clean you can hand washing the in the bathtub either afterwards or instead will work well.<P>Lay it out in the driveway afterwards to dry, or if you're going to be around to watch it and move it around you can lay it on the lawn and let it dry.  Don't leave it in any 1 spot too long on the lawn on a sunny day or you risk killing the grass underneath. <p>[This message has been edited by LarryB (edited 03-10-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000003||FieroLisa||03-10-2001||11:48 AM||||Thanks for the info, the cover is fairly clean, but I just got the car painted and when I do put the cover on it when I go down to Daytona, I don't want to risk having scratchy dirt and junk in it. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula88||03-10-2001||10:16 PM||||For my money, I'd machine wash it, but take it to a laundromat and use a large front loading machine - one that's not reciprocating.  It'll be easier on the material.||||reg||1
